{
  "answer": "APR stands for Annual Percentage Rate, which represents the yearly interest rate charged on your debt. In this case, with a 12 percent APR on a balance of 1,000,000 cents (or $10,000), the monthly interest rate is 1 percent (12 percent divided by 12 months). Applying that 1 percent monthly rate to your starting balance of $1,000 results in $10 of interest for the first month. Please note that no payment execution is available, money must be represented as integer cents, APR can range from 0 to 1000, time-varying payments are unsupported, and the projection model uses fixed APR and payments with monthly interest rounded to cents before a month-end payment.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "field": "aprPercent",
      "value": 12
    },
    {
      "field": "balanceCents",
      "value": 100000
    },
    {
      "field": "monthlyPaymentCents",
      "value": 60000
    }
  ]
}

